WEBVTT

01:23.660 --> 01:29.470
[LAZARUS]

01:38.250 --> 01:40.080
I did everything I could.

01:40.520 --> 01:42.150
The rest is up to them.

01:42.660 --> 01:43.890
Can they be saved?

01:44.070 --> 01:45.640
I don't know.

01:45.860 --> 01:46.949
It's a miracle

01:46.950 --> 01:50.030
that they're alive.

01:51.670 --> 01:56.060
[Episode 12: Close to the edge]

02:02.520 --> 02:03.610
You're awake.

02:05.440 --> 02:07.499
You came all the way here.

02:07.500 --> 02:09.389
You're something. Mad Screamer.

02:09.979 --> 02:11.339
Respect.

02:11.340 --> 02:13.500
You gradually found out who I am.

02:17.250 --> 02:19.099
I've been waiting for you.

02:19.100 --> 02:21.578
I thought you might come at some point.

02:21.579 --> 02:23.310
Me too.

02:23.680 --> 02:26.169
I want to see
Popcorn Wizard no matter what.

02:26.170 --> 02:26.990
Lin.

02:27.710 --> 02:29.800
This is my name.

02:29.900 --> 02:32.449
This is the first time
I've told anyone my name.

02:32.450 --> 02:34.130
My name is Eleina.

02:34.300 --> 02:35.479
By the way, Doug.

02:35.480 --> 02:36.470
What?

02:38.590 --> 02:40.040
Thank goodness.

02:40.460 --> 02:41.660
He's alive.

02:48.900 --> 02:50.200
Where am I?

03:08.220 --> 03:10.149
It looks like we're being watched.

03:10.150 --> 03:13.100
Anyway, it's still better
than just dying like that.

03:14.960 --> 03:17.840
I've never been hospitalized since then.

03:19.260 --> 03:21.740
[US Army INSCOM]

03:24.620 --> 03:26.420
I don't accept charity.

03:28.180 --> 03:29.730
Commander's order?

03:29.900 --> 03:34.140
[Washington D.C.]

03:30.050 --> 03:32.060
Is that even possible?

03:32.350 --> 03:33.649
No.

03:33.650 --> 03:36.600
But this is only one possibility.

03:36.910 --> 03:40.670
Your field is psychopathology, right?

03:40.810 --> 03:43.019
My field is human symbiosis studies.

03:43.020 --> 03:45.510
I have a task for you.

03:45.880 --> 03:47.339
I want you to investigate

03:47.340 --> 03:50.479
a Phantom Assassin known as Soryu.

03:50.480 --> 03:51.569
Soryu?

03:51.570 --> 03:52.510
Yes.

03:52.710 --> 03:57.230
This might be the key
to the whole incident.

04:04.760 --> 04:06.609
You're here to visit the patient, right?

04:06.610 --> 04:08.780
Yes, sorry.

04:43.060 --> 04:45.470
I was dreaming.

04:45.590 --> 04:46.450
Huh?

04:47.110 --> 04:49.110
I keep having the same dream.

04:49.680 --> 04:52.190
Falling endlessly, deeper and deeper,

04:52.520 --> 04:54.870
as if I'm about to
drop into another world.

04:55.620 --> 04:59.060
But there's always an angel who saves me.

05:00.800 --> 05:03.410
Was it you who saved me?

05:03.550 --> 05:05.660
Yes, don't you remember?

05:06.870 --> 05:09.640
Then... you're that angel.

05:10.640 --> 05:12.960
Wait, are you still half-asleep?

05:13.980 --> 05:14.980
Where is that guy?

05:15.140 --> 05:16.320
The assassin?

05:16.610 --> 05:17.640
He escaped.

05:17.880 --> 05:19.680
Looks like he was badly injured.

05:20.180 --> 05:21.440
I see.

05:23.320 --> 05:26.310
Until now, I've had
many brushes with death,

05:27.220 --> 05:30.110
but this is the first time
someone's saved me.

05:31.840 --> 05:33.380
I'll remember this favor.

05:35.200 --> 05:37.480
Under Leland's orders,

05:37.810 --> 05:40.839
this place is perfect
for treatment. No one will suspect a thing.

05:40.840 --> 05:43.039
By the way, he really did sleep for ages.

05:43.040 --> 05:44.210
Seriously.

05:44.670 --> 05:47.100
The world ended while you were sleeping.

05:48.620 --> 05:50.040
Right.

05:50.460 --> 05:52.139
But you can't push yourself yet.

05:52.140 --> 05:54.770
I have to protect the doctor, the witness.

05:55.300 --> 05:57.039
Don't get up.

05:57.040 --> 05:59.369
In your condition,
anyone else would already be dead.

05:59.370 --> 06:01.700
And besides... it's too late.

06:02.730 --> 06:05.130
The witness's body has already been found.

06:07.800 --> 06:11.320
[The White House]

06:09.020 --> 06:11.430
Abel, long time no see.

06:11.920 --> 06:13.649
How are you feeling?

06:13.650 --> 06:14.700
Commander.

06:15.020 --> 06:16.270
I know.

06:16.470 --> 06:18.059
Even though I took Hapna,

06:18.060 --> 06:20.319
I still thought I'd be fine.

06:20.320 --> 06:22.950
I admit I was overconfident.

06:23.460 --> 06:26.159
It's not the best timing to bring this up,

06:26.160 --> 06:28.910
but I actually came to ask a favor.

06:29.120 --> 06:30.560
I figured as much.

06:31.070 --> 06:32.080
In fact,

06:32.460 --> 06:34.620
two favors.

06:37.010 --> 06:38.289
You really

06:38.290 --> 06:40.020
can't be tamed, huh?

06:40.980 --> 06:42.209
But just a while ago,

06:42.210 --> 06:44.460
you and Mr. Abel seemed pretty close.

06:45.820 --> 06:47.000
You...

06:47.090 --> 06:50.550
Don't tell me you're actually Abel's spy.

06:53.550 --> 06:54.390
Huh?

06:54.620 --> 06:55.590
Huh?

06:55.820 --> 06:58.158
We met during the investigation committee.

06:58.159 --> 07:00.240
I'm Elizabeth from the NSA.

07:00.480 --> 07:01.919
A colleague of Abel's.

07:01.920 --> 07:03.509
Ah, I see.

07:03.510 --> 07:05.549
He's Dr. 909.

07:05.550 --> 07:07.929
Alias, Donald McDonald.

07:07.930 --> 07:08.920
Got it reversed.

07:10.370 --> 07:13.770
According to the plea bargain,
he's here to help us this time.

07:13.920 --> 07:15.349
I'll do anything.

07:15.350 --> 07:17.910
I really can't survive prison life.

07:18.110 --> 07:18.900
Hmm.

07:19.030 --> 07:20.519
Feels like I've seen you somewhere.

07:20.520 --> 07:22.290
Nope, never seen you at all.

07:22.410 --> 07:23.359
Hmm.

07:23.360 --> 07:25.330
I borrowed the hacker system.

07:31.330 --> 07:33.759
So that was you too, huh?

07:33.760 --> 07:36.309
The one who scattered

07:36.310 --> 07:37.930
all the tax evaders' money?

07:38.050 --> 07:39.399
Ah, yes.

07:39.400 --> 07:40.539
That's incredible.

07:40.540 --> 07:41.829
No, you're the amazing one.

07:41.830 --> 07:44.359
The one who
turned the Pentagon into a square.

07:44.360 --> 07:46.230
Haha, that one, huh.

07:46.380 --> 07:47.739
So...

07:47.740 --> 07:50.619
Did we accidentally make history or what?

07:50.620 --> 07:51.809
Don't you think that's kind of cool?

07:51.810 --> 07:53.120
Maybe it is.

08:00.710 --> 08:02.399
Has your fever gone down?

08:02.400 --> 08:04.340
Ah, I think so.

08:04.430 --> 08:05.639
That's great.

08:05.640 --> 08:08.859
Normally, a fever
from Hapna doesn't go away like that.

08:08.860 --> 08:10.509
Don't tell me you're immortal?

08:10.510 --> 08:12.319
Oh, right.

08:12.320 --> 08:13.579
What is it?

08:13.580 --> 08:17.379
I got caught up
in some incident once, nearly died.

08:17.380 --> 08:18.580
Seriously?

08:18.680 --> 08:21.650
That time, too,
I was the only one who survived.

08:21.880 --> 08:23.470
But I was just a kid then.

08:23.600 --> 08:25.400
Don't remember much clearly.

08:25.710 --> 08:27.560
You're still a kid now.

08:34.059 --> 08:35.960
Hey, Lin.

08:36.080 --> 08:38.489
There's something
I really need to ask you.

08:38.490 --> 08:39.610
What is it?

08:40.429 --> 08:42.298
Dr. Skinner is planning

08:42.299 --> 08:44.840
to use Hapna to destroy the world.

08:45.280 --> 08:46.639
You knew that.

08:46.640 --> 08:48.760
Why are you still helping him?

08:52.590 --> 08:56.009
The island I was
born on is near the Maldives.

08:56.010 --> 08:58.669
Many people
there have Congenital Analgesia.

08:58.670 --> 09:00.950
Of course, I have it too.

09:01.120 --> 09:02.500
Congenital Analgesia?

09:04.670 --> 09:07.540
Can't feel any pain at all.

09:07.930 --> 09:09.709
Researchers came to study

09:09.710 --> 09:11.080
the genetic trait.

09:11.350 --> 09:13.280
One of them was Skinner.

09:14.050 --> 09:17.850
He knew our island was sinking.

09:17.980 --> 09:20.839
And without saying
anything, he bought the island.

09:20.840 --> 09:23.459
None of us had money.

09:23.460 --> 09:26.460
We would've sunk with it.

09:26.600 --> 09:29.509
But with that money,
we were able to relocate elsewhere.

09:29.510 --> 09:32.739
Skinner did the same for many islands.

09:32.740 --> 09:34.240
Saved everyone.

09:35.190 --> 09:36.820
That's what I believe.

09:37.180 --> 09:39.350
For that man, I'd do anything.

09:39.740 --> 09:43.020
Even if it costs my life,
I'll protect him.

09:44.010 --> 09:44.930
Lin.

09:45.390 --> 09:46.779
As for what Skinner is thinking now,

09:46.780 --> 09:50.050
I honestly don't know.

09:50.390 --> 09:54.020
But he's not the kind of
man who'd sell his soul to the devil.

09:54.640 --> 09:57.220
That's something I've always believed.

10:00.060 --> 10:01.320
Hundun.

10:01.550 --> 10:03.480
Hmm? You've never heard of it?

10:03.590 --> 10:05.020
Nope.

10:05.950 --> 10:07.440
That guy said

10:07.810 --> 10:11.400
he'd show me what Hundun would become.

10:12.170 --> 10:15.500
Hundun, amazed
and wide-eyed, died in the end.

10:15.670 --> 10:17.620
[Hundun – a legendary
faceless deity from Chinese lore]

10:15.850 --> 10:17.530
That's what was written.

10:18.210 --> 10:19.730
But you...

10:19.830 --> 10:22.250
Were you chatting while fighting?

10:22.360 --> 10:23.220
Mm-hmm.

10:23.360 --> 10:24.640
By the way,

10:24.840 --> 10:28.109
if you're going to die,
at least leave your contact info first.

10:28.110 --> 10:30.539
Otherwise it's a pain
for the ones left behind.

10:30.540 --> 10:31.979
I don't have friends like that.

10:31.980 --> 10:33.549
That's not true, is it?

10:33.550 --> 10:35.399
You must have
at least one or two relatives.

10:35.400 --> 10:37.130
I've lived alone all this time.

10:38.570 --> 10:40.260
Speaking of which...

10:40.510 --> 10:41.700
Weren't you also...

10:49.760 --> 10:51.720
When I was a kid,

10:52.090 --> 10:53.500
I had a friend.

10:54.450 --> 10:56.750
I had no parents or siblings.

10:57.190 --> 10:59.780
He was like family to me.

11:00.440 --> 11:02.950
We even formed a gang-like group.

11:03.590 --> 11:06.390
Because without
doing that, we couldn't survive.

11:07.750 --> 11:08.880
And then?

11:09.190 --> 11:11.420
They all died.

11:12.170 --> 11:14.090
I was the only one who lived.

11:15.440 --> 11:17.800
This is something I kept from back then.

11:20.000 --> 11:21.239
After that,

11:21.240 --> 11:24.030
I decided never to make friends again.

11:24.530 --> 11:25.750
No matter where I go,

11:26.040 --> 11:28.670
I always move on before settling down.

11:29.870 --> 11:31.100
But,

11:31.970 --> 11:34.550
I think this place isn't so bad either.

11:42.530 --> 11:51.460
[Lazarus]

11:52.490 --> 11:56.820
NSA is going to forcibly
search the Army INSCOM?

11:57.100 --> 11:59.360
Never heard of such a thing.

11:59.550 --> 12:01.820
Of course, it's normally impossible.

12:02.010 --> 12:04.420
But there's one exception.

12:04.820 --> 12:08.350
A direct order from the Commander.

12:08.490 --> 12:10.160
I know it's asking a lot,

12:10.330 --> 12:11.609
but there's no other way

12:11.610 --> 12:14.240
to handle this crisis.

12:16.900 --> 12:18.210
Understood.

12:19.000 --> 12:20.189
Maybe

12:20.190 --> 12:23.590
this will be my final mission.

12:25.530 --> 12:28.609
Actually, before Hapna
even hit the market,

12:28.610 --> 12:31.500
when it was still
in clinical trials, I took it.

12:31.960 --> 12:34.860
I brought this on myself.

12:35.940 --> 12:38.450
I will definitely catch Skinner.

12:39.150 --> 12:42.210
And what about the other matter?

12:44.210 --> 12:46.180
What about information on Soryu?

12:46.280 --> 12:47.780
Absolutely nothing.

12:47.890 --> 12:49.519
All we found

12:49.520 --> 12:52.740
was footage of the Agent HQ.

12:50.320 --> 12:53.520
[Surveillance 16]

12:53.300 --> 12:54.430
As expected,

12:54.590 --> 12:57.409
it's Army Second
Lieutenant Schneider and Captain Hayes.

12:57.410 --> 13:00.359
But the most critical info on Soryu

13:00.360 --> 13:01.820
is nowhere to be found.

13:02.260 --> 13:04.829
I've searched everywhere,

13:04.830 --> 13:07.329
the dark web, private
databases, every corner.

13:07.330 --> 13:09.940
It's as if he doesn't exist at all.

13:10.450 --> 13:13.810
Maybe he really doesn't.

13:14.840 --> 13:16.069
I see.

13:16.070 --> 13:16.960
Huh.

13:16.600 --> 13:18.970
[Surveillance 16]

13:16.990 --> 13:18.319
Change the direction of the investigation.

13:18.320 --> 13:20.990
Start digging into Agent HQ.

13:21.140 --> 13:22.190
Understood.

13:23.640 --> 13:25.410
You've gone too far.

13:25.770 --> 13:28.370
There's no turning back now.

13:28.910 --> 13:31.459
What exactly happened?

13:31.460 --> 13:38.130
[Samuel Hayes]

13:31.770 --> 13:34.499
The reason you failed
to eliminate Axel Gilberto

13:34.500 --> 13:38.200
was because you hired
an unvetted assassin.

13:38.670 --> 13:40.160
And not only that,

13:40.430 --> 13:42.459
you detained Hersch,

13:42.460 --> 13:45.499
who noticed the troops
being dispatched to Pakistan.

13:45.500 --> 13:48.930
How do you plan to deal with this?

13:50.220 --> 13:52.749
That team called Lazarus,

13:52.750 --> 13:55.210
their goal isn't just to find Skinner.

13:55.640 --> 13:58.859
They're an organization
trying to expose our classified intel.

13:58.860 --> 14:00.660
That's become crystal clear.

14:01.430 --> 14:04.430
This situation has escalated to the level of warfare.

14:12.980 --> 14:16.390
[Unknown]

14:14.960 --> 14:16.340
HQ?

14:16.650 --> 14:19.000
Mind explaining the situation?

14:19.250 --> 14:21.260
You've stirred up a real mess.

14:21.700 --> 14:23.000
Do you realize

14:23.360 --> 14:25.450
we hired you to quietly

14:25.560 --> 14:27.989
push this operation forward?

14:27.990 --> 14:28.830
Shut up.

14:29.680 --> 14:31.889
This has nothing to do with the contract anymore.

14:31.890 --> 14:34.039
I'm going to kill that man no matter what.

14:34.040 --> 14:35.439
Saying it has nothing to do with the contract,

14:35.440 --> 14:38.030
do you know who you're talking to?

14:38.260 --> 14:39.360
You guys

14:39.560 --> 14:42.490
just want to wipe out the remnants in Arizona, right?

14:44.680 --> 14:50.560
[Unknown]

14:45.900 --> 14:47.469
What's wrong? Hey.

14:47.470 --> 14:48.570
I...

14:48.960 --> 14:50.500
Hey, what did you say?

14:56.400 --> 14:58.920
Who... am I?

15:00.920 --> 15:03.210
He's completely lost control.

15:03.460 --> 15:06.050
We don't know when he'll leak something.

15:06.790 --> 15:08.759
I'll report everything to my superior.

15:08.760 --> 15:10.920
I'm going to request your dismissal.

15:11.540 --> 15:13.320
We will inform you

15:13.530 --> 15:15.390
according to the formal process.

15:15.840 --> 15:17.200
That's all I have to say.

15:22.020 --> 15:24.740
[Abel Anderson]

15:28.900 --> 15:31.540
This is Skinner's artificial heart.

15:31.700 --> 15:32.720
It's beating.

15:32.870 --> 15:35.080
Which means he's still alive.

15:35.240 --> 15:38.349
The one who found Skinner said

15:38.350 --> 15:40.780
he's fine with us giving away his location.

15:41.140 --> 15:42.710
This place is...

15:42.890 --> 15:44.109
Babylonia.

15:44.110 --> 15:45.659
Near the command center.

15:45.660 --> 15:47.110
Huh?

15:47.460 --> 15:48.960
Abel's agent?

15:49.290 --> 15:50.980
Got it. And then?

15:51.250 --> 15:54.280
Don't tell me you saw the killer's face.

15:54.420 --> 15:56.189
I did. Saw it crystal clear.

15:56.190 --> 15:57.890
Return to HQ immediately.

15:58.020 --> 15:59.719
There's something I want you to compare it with.

15:59.720 --> 16:01.740
Got it. On my way.

16:03.440 --> 16:05.339
I'll leave this to Millie.

16:05.340 --> 16:07.170
I'm heading back to command.

16:07.350 --> 16:08.840
Mm, yeah.

16:09.320 --> 16:12.250
There's one day left until Skinner's announcement.

16:12.420 --> 16:15.260
This might be the last time I see you.

16:15.610 --> 16:16.979
Is that so?

16:16.980 --> 16:19.140
Any unfinished business?

16:20.860 --> 16:22.570
Nope.

16:23.110 --> 16:24.530
And you?

16:24.660 --> 16:25.689
Me?

16:25.690 --> 16:27.240
Unfinished business...

16:27.460 --> 16:28.460
Hmm, let me think.

16:41.360 --> 16:42.490
Well then, goodbye.

16:49.040 --> 16:51.030
[Abel Anderson]

16:54.210 --> 16:56.780
All personnel, move out immediately!

17:00.960 --> 17:02.580
It's too dangerous.

17:03.080 --> 17:05.358
Captain Hayes is plotting a rebellion.

17:05.359 --> 17:06.199
Huh?

17:06.200 --> 17:09.210
I was nearly killed too.

17:09.780 --> 17:11.399
Based on the evidence found at the scene.

17:11.400 --> 17:13.060
We'll leave the rest to you.

17:13.230 --> 17:14.069
Understood.

17:18.510 --> 17:19.630
Here, this way.

17:24.880 --> 17:25.789
Huh?

17:25.790 --> 17:27.109
I'll explain later.

17:27.280 --> 17:30.460
We need you to confirm if this man is the killer.

17:32.370 --> 17:34.530
It's him. No doubt about it.

17:34.820 --> 17:36.430
Just as we thought.

17:37.030 --> 17:39.440
This “HQ” person doesn't exist at all.

17:39.710 --> 17:41.170
Maybe this man

17:41.340 --> 17:43.379
has dissociative identity disorder.

17:43.380 --> 17:45.110
- Huh?
- What's that?

17:45.610 --> 17:48.659
When a personality is under extreme threat,

17:48.660 --> 17:52.460
another one can emerge in order to survive.

17:52.820 --> 17:54.750
You mean multiple personalities?

17:55.070 --> 17:56.269
If that's the case...

17:56.270 --> 17:57.890
It might be related.

17:58.110 --> 17:59.570
Axel said the man asked him

18:00.210 --> 18:02.340
if he knew something called “Hundun.”

18:02.860 --> 18:05.400
Could it be... the Hundun Project?

18:22.210 --> 18:24.530
I'm Abel Anderson from the NSA.

18:25.030 --> 18:28.160
As per the Commander's recent orders,

18:28.320 --> 18:31.939
we will be conducting an internal investigation of the Army INSCOM

18:31.940 --> 18:36.210
and arresting anyone suspected of concealing evidence.

18:36.490 --> 18:37.569
Well, well...

18:37.570 --> 18:39.990
So you're raiding the Army now?

18:40.470 --> 18:41.960
Where's Hayes?

18:44.620 --> 18:45.660
Tch.

19:04.720 --> 19:05.330
[DRW]

19:15.110 --> 19:16.210
What's wrong?

19:24.000 --> 19:24.960
Doug?

19:25.840 --> 19:26.840
You okay?

19:26.970 --> 19:29.320
Hey, Doug, get in, get in!

19:29.820 --> 19:30.830
She is...

19:30.960 --> 19:33.250
Ah, she's the Popcorn Wizard!

19:33.390 --> 19:34.290
Win.

19:35.180 --> 19:36.360
Also,

19:36.580 --> 19:38.110
return Hersch to us.

19:38.340 --> 19:39.280
Oh?

19:39.430 --> 19:42.020
You really want to go to war over this?

19:42.390 --> 19:45.110
You'd go this far just to rescue Hersch?

19:45.640 --> 19:47.809
If you won't hand him over, I'll go get him myself.

19:47.810 --> 19:50.610
That person you're talking about never came here.

19:52.990 --> 19:54.400
Just kidding.

19:54.650 --> 19:55.639
So,

19:55.640 --> 19:58.779
what do we get in return?

19:58.780 --> 20:00.360
In return?

20:00.820 --> 20:02.690
Cut the nonsense.

20:06.020 --> 20:07.930
Where's Skinner?

20:08.130 --> 20:10.860
In the Wanderer's Settlement in Babylonia City.

20:10.960 --> 20:13.490
Seriously? That's nearby!

20:13.820 --> 20:15.820
But the area's pretty big.

20:15.930 --> 20:18.330
We don't have time to search house by house.

20:18.660 --> 20:19.599
Looks like

20:19.600 --> 20:22.820
we'll need some kind of sign to find Skinner.

20:23.070 --> 20:24.059
What about Axel?

20:24.060 --> 20:25.890
He's not able to move yet.

20:26.140 --> 20:29.110
Then let's try reaching out to Gil.

20:29.440 --> 20:32.220
Any clues or signs?

20:32.890 --> 20:34.800
Eleina, we need to go right away.

20:34.920 --> 20:37.679
But there might be an ambush waiting at the airport.

20:37.680 --> 20:39.399
Then let's use that to our advantage.

20:39.400 --> 20:40.750
Already taken care of.

20:41.230 --> 20:42.849
- Where to turn left?
- Huh?

20:42.850 --> 20:45.310
Got it!

20:45.940 --> 20:47.370
Hang on tight!

20:56.810 --> 20:57.300
[Road Closed]

21:08.810 --> 21:10.550
[Islamabad Hypercube Terminal]

21:11.220 --> 21:15.760
[Pakistan Hypercube Terminal]

21:12.820 --> 21:13.900
This is...

21:14.250 --> 21:17.720
The soon-to-open Hypercube Terminal.

21:18.210 --> 21:20.070
I applied for special clearance.

21:22.150 --> 21:23.480
You're Mr. Doug, right?

21:23.730 --> 21:25.529
You've been cleared in advance.

21:25.530 --> 21:27.069
Everything's operational?

21:27.070 --> 21:28.399
We can move at top speed.

21:28.400 --> 21:30.740
It should've been running already,

21:30.900 --> 21:33.310
but the Hapna incident delayed it.

21:33.670 --> 21:35.680
Well then, goodbye, Eleina.

21:36.360 --> 21:37.930
- Lin.
- Here.

21:38.840 --> 21:41.940
Which one's the line that only connects to me?

21:42.070 --> 21:42.900
Huh?

21:43.200 --> 21:44.609
No matter where you are,

21:44.610 --> 21:46.959
you're my greatest rival,

21:46.960 --> 21:48.440
and my best friend.

21:51.400 --> 21:54.490
Bye now. Take care of the Skinner matter.

21:54.580 --> 21:56.980
I'll definitely find him.

21:59.280 --> 22:00.190
Let's go.

22:00.320 --> 22:02.180
We'll be at Skinner's place soon.

22:12.510 --> 22:15.459
[We'll meet where angels dwell]

22:15.460 --> 22:17.530
[Countdown: 1 day]

23:50.090 --> 23:54.920
[Next Episode: Episode 13
The World Is Yours]
